# ===================================================================
# Insurance Portal - database connection (YOUR OWN Supabase project)
# ===================================================================
# 1. Copy this file to ".env"   ->   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in the three values below with your OWN Supabase project's details.
# 3. Run the app (see README). application.properties auto-loads this .env,
#    so you do NOT need to export any shell variables.
#
# ".env" is gitignored and must NEVER be committed - it holds your password.
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to find these values
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then:
#   Dashboard -> your project -> Project Settings -> Database
#     -> "Connection string" tab -> "JDBC"      gives SUPABASE_DB_URL
#     -> the "Connection pooler" host/user       (recommended - IPv4 friendly)
#     -> "Database password" is the one you set when creating the project
#        (use "Reset database password" if you don't remember it)
#
# The app creates all the tables automatically on first run, so a fresh,
# empty project is all you need.

# --- Connection pooler (Supavisor), session mode - recommended, works over IPv4 ---
# Replace <your-project-ref> and <region> with your project's values.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
SUPABASE_DB_USER=postgres.<your-project-ref>
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=your-database-password-here

# --- Alternative: direct connection (IPv6-only; times out on many IPv4 networks) ---
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://db.<your-project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# SUPABASE_DB_USER=postgres
